  "title": "Bump the samples to Web Chat 4.19.3-main.20261105.058fca6",
  "body": "> Clears 8 Dependabot alerts on `samples/package-lock.json`, which pins `botframework-webchat@4.19.1-main.20260529`.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- 🏫 Samples: bumped [`botframework-webchat@4.19.3-main.20261105.058fca6`](https://npmjs.com/package/botframework-webchat/v/4.19.3-main.20261105.058fca6), clearing `sanitize-html`, `valibot` and `katex` security alerts, in PR [#6019](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6019), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe samples' pinned May nightly still resolves `sanitize-html@2.17.4`, `valibot@1.3.1` and `katex@0.16.45`. They now pin `4.19.3-main.20261105.058fca6`, which has #5987 and #6001.\n\n## Design\n\n- Bumped the pin instead of adding `overrides`, which the next `npm run bump` would drop anyway.\n- Resolved with `--min-release-age=7`, exempting only the Web Chat packages and `@angular/*` (Speech SDK 1.17.0 peers, kept at 22.2.4), so the nightly is the only new version under 7 days old.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- 9 sample `package.json` files: `botframework-webchat` (and `botframework-webchat-api` in `f.selectable-activity`) on `4.19.3-main.20261105.058fca6`\n- `samples/package-lock.json`: `sanitize-html@2.18.1`, `valibot@1.4.2`, `katex@0.19.1`; drops `deepmerge`\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
